00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.080
BONDS BONDS BONDS:
Have you noticed that everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:08.120
has been buying bonds? In fact, so many people&nbsp;
have been buying bonds that the United States&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:14.320
archaic bond buying website, treasury direct, has&nbsp;
been crashing due to the traffic spikes. And it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:21.160
not just retail investors who want in either. In&nbsp;
fact, retail investors only account for about 7%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:27.480
of the bond market’s trading volume. Aka, more&nbsp;
than 90% of bonds are being traded by financial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:32.520
institutions and companies, and when you take a&nbsp;
look at the balance sheets of some of the largest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:38.480
companies in the world, this makes a lot of sense.&nbsp;
Take Apple for instance. They’re currently holding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:44.120
$34 billion in short term marketable securities&nbsp;
and $104 billion in long term marketable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:49.880
securities most of which is bonds and other fixed&nbsp;
income assets. Similarly, Microsoft is holding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:56.440
$104 billion in cash, cash equivalents, and short&nbsp;
term investments. Even Facebook who is generally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:01.760
the most willing to take massive risks like their&nbsp;
$100 billion bet on the Metaverse and $33 billion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:08.640
bet on AI has been buying up bonds. In fact, as of&nbsp;
their last quarterly report, Facebook was holding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:15.000
just over $53 billion in cash, cash equivalents,&nbsp;
and marketable securities. It’s not just these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.160
big tech companies that are investing heavily in&nbsp;
bonds either. Some of the most legendary investors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:26.080
of all time like Warren Buffett are buying bonds&nbsp;
hand over fist. In fact, Warren Buffett came into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:33.640
2023 holding $95 billion in treasury bills alone.&nbsp;
And as of August 2023, he was buying $10 billion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:47.064
worth of treasury bills every single week. So, why&nbsp;
in the world is everyone suddenly buying bonds?

00:01:47.064 --> 00:01:49.280
